            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0141" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg65"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4331/58: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at St. John’s</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Quarton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                John’s</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-09T17:00:00-02:30">April 9, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Sir John Hope-Simpson, Commissioner for Natural Resources, advised me today that
                    both he and the Dominions Office expressed an interest in opening negotiations
                    for a possible Newfoundland-United States trade treaty. He is planning to go to
                    Washington to consult with the British Embassy regarding the matter in June or
                    July. He would make the trip at once but feels that the Newfoundland case which
                    has been left to the Newfoundland Board of Trade has not been thoroughly
                    prepared and believes the next 2 months spent in investigations could be well
                    used. He is writing to the British Embassy expressing his views.</p>
                <p>Please forward questionnaire comprehending information desired for trade treaty
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quarton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
